      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3004452321,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Personally, I think:\n\n```\ncsf_to_add = (float)1.0 / (1 << iq_width);\n```\n\nis clearer. Since the spec says 2^-iq_width, and 2^x == (1 \\<\\< x); 2^-x == 1 / (1 \\<\\< x).\n\nBut you can think of these mathy things in different ways. And since you are the main maintainer of this code, it will probably be more consistent if your way of thinking is present throughout. So it bounces back to you to decide :smiley:",
          "author": {
            "id": 32613582,
            "username": "herr.thomas.magnusson",
            "public_email": null,
            "name": "Thomas Magnusson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f2cb43e0216bfe535c02c677fee6889a4052ddd2c4bcb6167d6cb9b7f9ce24da?s=80&d=identicon",
